          "filename": "Cymer Abbey (8370110370).jpg",
          "caption": "The Cistercian abbey of Cymer was founded in 1198-9. It was not very wealthy and lacks several features of a more traditional abbey. For example no trancepts were built and thus the tower (since collapsed) was built in the 14th century at the west end. Only the foundation lines of the monastic buildings to the south still exist although some of the abbey guesthouse walls are believed to survive in the current farmhouse.",
